    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d885">

                <pb facs="0874" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conference 184.01602/57a:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Naval Station
                        at Constantinople</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-07T22:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1919—10
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>384. For Berry, Ekaterinodar.</p>
                <p>Current reports here state 200 Russians repatriated from France mutinied at
                    Novorossiisk and were exterminated. Can you cable <pb facs="0875" n="763"
                        xml:id="pg763"/> facts? Has any word of the Allied note to Kolchak<anchor
                        n="14" xml:id="d885-f1"/> been received at Ekaterinodar and if so what is
                    the attitude of the Volunteer Army and the Kouban Government?</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
